        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 12, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, March 31, 2018</p><p>ORD C35580 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17D.050">Chapter 17D.050</a> REPEALED (Roadway Naming) </p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.010">Section 17D.050.010</a> REPEALED (Naming of Roadways – Procedure)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.020">Section 17D.050.020</a> REPEALED (Naming of Roadways – Policy)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.030">Section 17D.050.030</a> REPEALED (Street Addresses – Procedure)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.040">Section 17D.050.040</a> REPEALED (Street Addresses – Policy)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.050">Section 17D.050.050</a> REPEALED (Display of Addresses)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.060">Section 17D.050.060</a> REPEALED (Roadway Naming Appeals – Procedure)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050.070">Section 17D.050.070</a> REPEALED (Decision Criteria – Roadway Name Change)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35452 Section 1</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=17D.050A">Chapter 17D.050A</a> Roadway Naming and Addressing</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050A.010">Section 17D.050A.010</a> Purpose, Goals, and Intent<br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The purpose and intent of this chapter is to establish a uniform method for naming roadways and assigning addresses for real property and structures within the City of Spokane.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The goals of this chapter are as follows:</p>
        		<ol>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					To facilitate the expedient emergency response by medical, law enforcement, fire, rescue, and any other emergency services;</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					To regulate the display of property address numbers and provide for accurate road name signage, installation, and maintenance thereof; and</p>
        			</li>
        			<li>
        				<p>
        					To provide property owners, the general public, emergency responders, and government agencies and departments with an accurate and systematic means of identifying and locating property</p>
        			</li>
        		</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050A.020">Section 17D.050A.020</a> Applicability<br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			This chapter applies to all public and private roadways, addresses for real property, and structures situated within the City of Spokane.&nbsp; The City of Spokane may name or rename roadways and assign or reassign addresses as necessary to further the purpose of this chapter.&nbsp;</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			This chapter applies to the assignment of addresses to all new or existing buildings or properties within the City of Spokane.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			All non-conforming addresses may be changed to conform to this Code.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050A.030">Section 17D.050A.030</a> Administration<br />
        <p>
        	The Development Services Center shall administer the provisions of this chapter, unless otherwise provided for herein.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 14, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, December 22, 2016</p><p>ORD C35452 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=17D.050A.040">Section 17D.050A.040</a> Definitions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Limited Application.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Definitions provided here are given solely for purposes of administering this chapter. The Administrator may refer to definitions provided in SMC 17A.020 in the absence of a specific definition within this chapter, or for further clarity.</span></p>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Definitions.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Address&rdquo; means a property location identification with the following format, and typically in the following order:&nbsp; address number, directional prefix, roadway name, roadway type, building designator, and unit designator (e.g., &ldquo;123 W. Main St., Apt. 456&rdquo;).&nbsp; The following elements are required: address number, roadway name, and roadway type.&nbsp; The following elements may be optional:&nbsp; directional prefix, building designator, and unit designator.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Addressing Authority&rdquo; means the Development Services Center. </span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Address Number&rdquo; means the numeric designation for an addressable structure or unit.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Addressable&rdquo; means a property required to be assigned an address under this chapter.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Addressable Property, Addressable Structures, Addressable Sites or Addressable Units&rdquo; means, generally, the habitable or legally occupied structure, or a lot, parcel, or tract, but may also include other structures or sites as determined necessary by the relevant addressing authority.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Addressing Database&rdquo; means the computerized format for tracking assigned roadway names and addresses within the City of Spokane. </span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="7">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Addressing Grid System&rdquo; is the address number and directional system in a particular area such as a grid system, block system, plat, or subdivision.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="8">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Administrator&rdquo; means the Development Services Center Manager.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="9">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Building Designator&rdquo; means a single character alphabetic descriptor for a single building within a multiple unit complex (e.g., &ldquo;123 W. Main St., Bldg. A&rdquo;).</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="10">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Department&rdquo; means the Development Services Center.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="11">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Directional Prefix&rdquo; means a single or double character alphabetic descriptor within a roadway name consisting of any combination of the cardinal directions of North, South, East, and West, generally used in specific roadway naming schemes (i.e., N, S, E, W, NE, NW, SE, SW).</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="12">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;E911 Director&rdquo; means the manager of the local 911 service.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="13">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Non-conforming Address or Roadway Name&rdquo; means an address or roadway name that is not in compliance with this chapter.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="14">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Multiple Units&rdquo; means the presence of two or more addressable structures, addressable sites, or addressable units on a single Spokane County tax parcel or group of undivided interest parcels.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="15">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Multiple Unit Complex&rdquo; means an apartment, condominium, or business complex where there exist multiple buildings on a single site, and two or more buildings include multiple units.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="16">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Multiple Unit Structure&rdquo; means a single structure which contains two or more units.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="17">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Non-conforming Roadway Name Sign&rdquo; means a roadway name sign that is not in compliance with this chapter.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="18">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Regional Public Safety Spatial Database&rdquo; means the spatial format for tracking all assigned roadway names and addresses within Spokane County. This system is maintained by the Regional Public Safety Geographic Information Systems (RPSGIS) Committee for use in countywide public safety-related applications.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="19">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Roadway&rdquo; means a public or private way on which vehicles travel, encompassing all roadway types.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="20">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Roadway Name&rdquo; means the word or words either existing, or in the case of new or renamed roadways, which are approved by the Development Services Center, used in conjunction with a directional prefix, and/or a roadway type to identify a public or private roadway.</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="21">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Roadway Type&rdquo; means an abbreviated word used in conjunction with a roadway name to describe the character of the roadway and will be in accordance with USPS Publication No. 28 Appendix C1. The following are allowable roadway types:</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Alley (Aly): a narrow service roadway that serves rear lots and where platted width is less than twenty feet.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Avenue (Ave): a through local, collector or arterial roadway generally running east-west.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Boulevard (Blvd):&nbsp; a roadway with exceptional width, length and scenic value, typically with a landscaped median dividing the roadway; or an arterial or major collector roadway that lies diagonally to the east-west, north-south grid system.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Circle (Cir): a local or collector roadway having ingress and egress from the same roadway. See also &ldquo;Loop&rdquo;.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="5" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Court (Ct): a dead end or cul-de-sac that will not become an extension or a continuation of either an existing or future roadway, not longer than six hundred feet in length.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="6" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Drive (Dr): a lengthy collector or arterial that does not have a definite directional course.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="7" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Highway (Hwy): used to designate state or federal roadways only.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="8" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Lane (Ln): a roadway used as a private local access within a development.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Loop (Loop): a local or collector roadway having ingress and egress from the same roadway. See also &quot;Circle&rdquo;.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="10" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Parkway (Pkwy): a thoroughfare designated as a collector or arterial, with a median reflecting the park-like character implied in the name.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="11" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Place (Pl): a permanently dead-end roadway, terminating in a cul-de-sac, or short through roadway, not longer than six hundred fifty feet in length.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="12" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Road (Rd): typically reserved for roadways located outside the boundary of a city or town, and may be found within city/town limits due to past annexations or when a new roadway is in alignment with or within one hundred twenty five feet of an existing county road.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="13" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Street (St): a through local, collector or arterial roadway generally running north-south.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="14" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Way (Way): a curvilinear roadway.</span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="22">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Unit&rdquo; means a specific dwelling or commercial space amongst a larger group of dwellings or commercial spaces (e.g., apartment, suites, etc.).</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="23">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Unit Designator&rdquo; means a secondary address number that is used to identify a separate unit on a single lot, parcel, tract of land, or within a multiple unit complex. A unit designator at a minimum shall consist of a unit type and a numeric identifier (e.g., 10126 W. Rutter Pkwy., Apt. 2).&nbsp; See also: &ldquo;Multiple Units&rdquo;, &ldquo;Multiple Unit Complex&rdquo;, &ldquo;Multiple Unit Structure&rdquo;)</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="24">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">&ldquo;Unit Type&rdquo; means an abbreviated word used in conjunction with a unit designator to describe the character of the unit and will be in accordance with USPS Publication No. 28 Appendix C2.&nbsp; The following are allowable unit types:</span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
